## ACF field renaming/deletion — standing rule
Changing an ACF field's Name (not Label) after real data exists
detaches the existing data from view (not delete — still in
`wp_postmeta` under the old key, recoverable, but invisible to
`get_fields()` until fixed). Same caution applies to deleting a field:
data isn't lost but can be orphaned. Label changes are always safe.
Before any Name change or field deletion, check whether any events
actually hold data under that key
(`wp post meta get <id> <field_name> --allow-root`) and flag it to the
user rather than assuming.
